            title: "Octal Notation",
            body: "Permissions can be written as octal digits that sum together: 4=read, 2=write, 1=execute. e.g. `chmod 700 file` gives the owner all permissions and group/others none; `chmod 744 file` gives the owner all permissions and group/others read only. Full table: 0=--- 1=--x 2=-w- 3=-wx 4=r-- 5=r-x 6=rw- 7=rwx.",
